4 1145 "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$ Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of ${P}_{C\\to B}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C} & ={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot (-1)-(-2)\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =(-\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374005 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374006 13194139535910 true] [17592186374005 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374007 13194139535910 true] [17592186374005 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374008 13194139535910 true] [17592186374005 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374009 13194139535910 true] [17592186374005 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374010 13194139535910 true] [17592186374005 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535910 true] [17592186374005 1041 "selection" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374005 1104 #edb/ref 17592186374007 13194139535910 true] [17592186374005 1110 #uuid "0bb1ea54-9a3d-51c5-9e85-a16a7bd07ce3" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374006 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374006 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535910 true] [17592186374006 1111 #uuid "eb569263-df53-582c-947a-0456dce3ea40" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374007 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374007 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535910 true] [17592186374007 1111 #uuid "1f1df4b9-9903-53c2-8781-f1911fd9b550" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374008 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374008 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535910 true] [17592186374008 1111 #uuid "801a8750-078f-5d46-aec2-63c847d08218" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374009 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374009 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535910 true] [17592186374009 1111 #uuid "fe308c27-fbc3-5982-8d48-8b313bcd2a3b" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374010 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374010 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535910 true] [17592186374010 1111 #uuid "38a19ca9-b831-5bb7-83cc-f56bc01bb904" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374011 1017 #edb/ref 17592186374012 13194139535910 true] [17592186374011 1089 "q-35689" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374011 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535910 true] [17592186374011 1100 "Let $B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}$ and $C={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}$ be bases of ${R}^{2}.$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374011 1113 #uuid "8f8f7997-5431-5c08-819e-4fce158922f7" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374011 1145 "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ and $C$ as ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ and ${{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$, respectively.\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $C$ relative to the basis $B.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ relative to the basis $B.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we simply reduce the left-hand side to reduced row-echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the right-hand side, we obtain the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{C\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374012 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374013 13194139535910 true] [17592186374012 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374014 13194139535910 true] [17592186374012 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374015 13194139535910 true] [17592186374012 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374016 13194139535910 true] [17592186374012 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374017 13194139535910 true] [17592186374012 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535910 true] [17592186374012 1041 "selection" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374012 1104 #edb/ref 17592186374014 13194139535910 true] [17592186374012 1110 #uuid "8c0766a9-a4b4-5927-8a5a-32dc01fe7659" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374013 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374013 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535910 true] [17592186374013 1111 #uuid "ed058997-8ad5-54c2-8557-0e8e16b8f9ce" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374014 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374014 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535910 true] [17592186374014 1111 #uuid "2b5dc9ea-bafd-54dc-bdc2-68a8171405b6" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374015 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -9\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374015 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535910 true] [17592186374015 1111 #uuid "30a9b801-aeb8-5ab8-a393-2cde0442b1b7" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374016 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374016 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535910 true] [17592186374016 1111 #uuid "7a4974c8-d520-508d-ae18-8ef5622aab4e" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374017 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374017 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535910 true] [17592186374017 1111 #uuid "1216c78b-ab54-5b03-a07f-676894944c33" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374018 1017 #edb/ref 17592186374019 13194139535910 true] [17592186374018 1089 "q-81847" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374018 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535910 true] [17592186374018 1100 "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of ${R}^{2}.$ \nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to S}$ from $B$ to $S$ if \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374018 1113 #uuid "62dadad6-bc72-59c3-b335-faab5922669e" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374018 1145 "Recall  that the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$ consists of the vectors ${e}_{1}$ and ${e}_{2},$ given by\n\n$$\n{e}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{e}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe components of the vectors of $B$ are just the coordinates relative to the standard basis:\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,[{b}_{2}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $S.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 11\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535910 true] [17592186374019 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374020 13194139535910 true] [17592186374019 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374021 13194139535910 true] [17592186374019 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374022 13194139535910 true] [17592186374019 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374023 13194139535910 true] [17592186374019 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374024 13194139535910 true] [17592186374019 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535910 true] [17592186374019 1041 "selection" 13194139535910 true